-- `Refines` defines a refined command — adjectives applied to another command.


-- The plain form: a property added to an existing type.
[\(nonempty)::set]
Refines: X
satisfies:
. exists: x is \element:of{X}
  suchThat: x "in" X
Documented:
. adjective: "nonempty"
Id: "dff130c9-4fc4-4bd5-a7b0-dd6ee7a1ff23"


[\(commutative)::magma]
Refines: M ::= (X, *)
satisfies: M is \magma
Documented:
. adjective: "commutative"
Id: "b6c0c765-d12c-437c-80e1-7a0113e8b789"


-- `specifies:` names the refinement this one inherits from. `implicitly:` says
-- the group only restates that inherited clause...
[\(nonempty)::magma]
Refines: M ::= (X, *)
implicitly:
specifies: M is \(nonempty)::set
Documented:
. adjective: "nonempty"
Id: "9411125d-e05c-41ff-9b1e-fc55f9547604"


-- ...and `explicitly:` says it adds at least one property of its own.
[\(nonempty)::monoid]
Refines: M ::= (X, *, e)
explicitly:
specifies: M is \(nonempty)::magma
satisfies: M is \monoid
Documented:
. adjective: "nonempty"
Id: "aeda535b-696d-426a-916c-da930f1d5d94"


-- A refined spec-infix command.
[A \:(proper)::subset:/ B]
Refines: A
when: B is \set
Documented:
. adjective: "proper"
Id: "9d1238e3-30db-4e78-a3ac-e53ccf6dd887"


-- A refinement of the base type is available on its subtypes, so a nonempty
-- group is reachable through `\group`'s chain up to `\set`.
Theorem:
given: G ::= (X, *, e) is \group
where: G is? \(nonempty)::monoid
then: G is? \(nonempty)::magma
Documented:
. called: "refinements follow the subtype chain"
Id: "7474854b-5143-4d83-a0bb-50e943ace450"
